==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|peine}},
from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|poena}},
from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|ποινή||penalty, fine, bloodmoney}}. {{doublet|en|pain}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|legal}} [[pain|Pain]] or [[punishment]].

====Usage notes====
This is only used in common law legal contexts, as part of {{w|Law French}}, most often in the phrase {{m|en|peine forte et dure||strong and hard pain}}.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|peine forte et dure}}

